# Build-context trimming for the ONE image whose context is the repo root:
# backend/Dockerfile.worker (see railway.toml for why the worker's archive root is the repo
# root and not backend/).
#
# Docker reads the .dockerignore at the CONTEXT root, so this file does not affect
# backend/Dockerfile, backend/Dockerfile.prod or the frontend images -- their contexts are
# backend/ and frontend/, which have their own .dockerignore files.
#
# On Railway the upload has already been trimmed by .gitignore and .railwayignore; this
# matters for a local `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile.worker .`, where without it the
# daemon is handed node_modules, virtualenvs and the whole git history.

.git
.github
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
.venv311
**/.venv311
frontend/dist
frontend/build
frontend/coverage
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
frontend/.browser-harness
backend/nesting-runtime
landing/dist
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.hypothesis
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov
*.log
*.db

# Local configuration, credentials and runtime data never belong in an image.
# Repeat these rules in each context's .dockerignore; Docker does not inherit them.
**/.env*
**/*.env
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
**/.venv*
**/venv
**/env
**/.aws
**/.azure
**/.ssh
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/pip.conf
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal
**/*.sqlite3-shm
**/*.sqlite3-wal
**/uploads
**/logs
**/backups
**/.DS_Store
